{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S4: Config-driven link-relation mapping, skip-not-approximate preserved\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nEpic 3d7a adds a config-driven mapping seam. S1 landed the core\n`mapping_config.py` (`MappingLayer` with `link_map: Mapping[str,str]`,\n`SKIP=\"skip\"`, `resolve_for_project`, `validate`, `Capability`). S2 made STATUS\nconfig-driven (`config.effective_status_map`, `config.py:77`). S4 does the same\nfor rebar-relation → Jira-link mapping while preserving \"skip, don't approximate\":\nmap to a real declared project link type, or skip — never invent an approximate\nlink.\n\nToday rebar→Jira link emission is hardcoded. The per-dep skip/emit decision lives\nin `outbound_links.py::_diff_links` (`outbound_links.py:34`): it calls\n`links.link_payload_for_relation(relation)` (`:83`) and, when that returns `None`,\n`continue`s — the skip (`:84`). `_diff_links` is called only from the UPDATE path,\n`outbound_mutation_builders.py:285` (creates emit no links). The\n`SupportsLinks.link_payload_for_relation` capability is implemented in TWO\nbackends, each reading the built-in `RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK` directly:\n\n- `adapters/jira/backend.py:320` → `return RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK.get(relation)` (`:323`, import `:29`)\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:526` → `return RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK.get(relation)` (`:527`, import `:26`)\n\nBuilt-in default `RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK: dict[str, tuple[str, bool]]`\n(`adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py:104`): `blocks→(Blocks,False)`,\n`depends_on→(Blocks,True)`, `relates_to→(Relates,False)`. Deliberately unsynced\nrelations are `UNSYNCED_RELATIONS` (`value_maps.py:128`: duplicates, supersedes,\ndiscovered_from, caused_by). Parent relationships are OUT of scope (S7).\n\nTYPE MISMATCH to reconcile: built-in payload is a `(link_type, swap)` TUPLE and\n`link_payload_for_relation` returns `(vendor_type, swap)`; the S1 `link_map` axis\nis a flat `str→str` map (`mapping_config.py:98`).\n\n## Approach\n\nMirror S2's forward seam exactly.\n\n1. **New `config.effective_link_map(project_key, root)` in `config.py`** (NEW),\n   analogous to `effective_status_map` (`config.py:77`). Add a second string literal\n   `local_to_jira_link: dict[str,str]` = `{\"blocks\":\"Blocks\",\"depends_on\":\"Blocks\",\n   \"relates_to\":\"Relates\"}` (the link-TYPE component only; `config.py` stays\n   adapter-free, kept honest by a parity test — same pattern as `local_to_jira_status`).\n   Build `builtin = mc.MappingLayer(link_map=local_to_jira_link)`, resolve via\n   `mc.resolve_for_project(cfg, project_key, builtin=builtin)`, then\n   `mc.validate(resolved, mc.Capability(has_link_types=True))` (fail-closed) and\n   return `resolved.link_map` — **retaining `SKIP` entries** (unlike status, which\n   drops them) so a forced skip is distinguishable from an absent key.\n\n2. **Thread the effective link map into `_diff_links`.** Add\n   `_effective_link_map_for(ticket, mapping, repo_root)` in `outbound_differ.py`\n   (NEW, sibling of `_effective_status_map_for`, `:272`) resolving the project via\n   `projects_store.resolve_project` then calling `config.effective_link_map`. Pass\n   its result as a new optional `link_map: Mapping[str,str] | None = None` arg to\n   `_diff_links`/`_diff_link_removals` (`outbound_links.py:34,120`); compute it at\n   `outbound_mutation_builders.py:285` beside `_status_map` and pass it in.\n\n3. **Tuple-vs-string reconciliation rule (in `_diff_links`, after `payload =\n   links.link_payload_for_relation(relation)`):**\n   - `override = link_map.get(relation)` (None when no config / absent key).\n   - `override == SKIP` → `continue` (force-skip; never approximate).\n   - `override` is a `str` → `vendor_type = override`, **`swap = payload[1] if\n     payload else False`** — config overrides ONLY the link_type component, the\n     built-in swap flag is preserved; a newly-mapped unsynced relation defaults\n     `swap=False` (direction-agnostic).\n   - `override is None` → today's behaviour: use `payload`, and if `payload is None`\n     `continue` (built-in unsynced skip).\n   With no `[mapping]` block the seam is inert — byte-for-byte today's emission.\n\n4. **Fail-closed on undeclared link type (#4).** The S1 mechanism already exists:\n   `MappingLayer.link_types` vocabulary (`mapping_config.py:102`), `Capability.\n   has_link_types` (`:80`), and `validate()`'s `_check_vocab(resolved.link_map,\n   resolved.link_types, ...)` (`:359`). A project declares its vocabulary as\n   `[mapping.default] link_types = [...]` (or per-project `[mapping.projects.KEY]\n   link_types`); `effective_link_map` calling `validate()` (NEW call site — S1's\n   `validate` is not yet invoked anywhere) raises `MappingConfigError` when any\n   `link_map` value is outside the declared `link_types`. `SKIP` is always allowed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `config.py`: add `local_to_jira_link` literal + `effective_link_map`. (~100→~130 LOC)\n- `outbound_differ.py`: add `_effective_link_map_for`.\n- `outbound_links.py`: add `link_map` arg + composition rule in `_diff_links`\n  (and pass-through to `_diff_link_removals`). (178→~200 LOC)\n- `outbound_mutation_builders.py`: compute + pass `link_map` at the `_diff_links`\n  call (`:285`).\n- Backends UNCHANGED: they keep returning the built-in payload; config composition\n  is layered ABOVE both via `link_map` (routes both consumers through one seam).\n- NEW test file `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_link_mapping.py`.\n- OUT of scope: parent relationships (S7), inbound link translation, priority/type axes.\n- All touched modules stay well under the 800-LOC hard cap.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_link_mapping.py` (`pytestmark =\npytest.mark.unit`), driving REAL entry points (`config.effective_link_map` and\n`outbound_links._diff_links`) via a tmp `rebar.toml` `[mapping]` block, asserting\nobservable behaviour only (resolved map + emitted mutation dicts / skips):\n\n- `test_link_config_effect` — a project `link_map` override (e.g. `relates_to =\n  \"Relationship\"`) changes the emitted `_diff_links` mutation's `type` while the\n  built-in `swap` is preserved; no `[mapping]` block ⇒ built-in emission unchanged.\n- `test_link_skip_preserved` — `link_map` value `\"skip\"` for a mapped relation\n  emits NO link mutation, and an unsynced relation (e.g. `supersedes`) still emits\n  nothing; no approximate link is ever substituted.\n- `test_link_undeclared_fails_closed` — a `link_map` value outside a declared\n  `link_types` vocabulary makes `effective_link_map` raise `MappingConfigError`\n  (fail-closed).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_diff_links` emission composes the config `link_map` over the backend\n      payload per the rule above (config overrides link_type, preserves built-in\n      swap); verified by `test_link_config_effect`.\n- [ ] \"Skip, don't approximate\" preserved: a `\"skip\"` override and unsynced\n      relations emit no link; verified by `test_link_skip_preserved`.\n- [ ] Undeclared link type fails closed against the declared `link_types`\n      vocabulary via `validate()`; verified by `test_link_undeclared_fails_closed`.\n- [ ] Both consumers (`adapters/jira/backend.py:323`,\n      `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:527`) are routed through the single\n      `effective_link_map` seam; no `[mapping]` block leaves emission byte-for-byte\n      unchanged.\n- [ ] A parity test keeps `config.local_to_jira_link` in lock-step with\n      `value_maps.RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`'s link-type components.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787353729534741001,"uuid":"2bb8b270-e0ba-438d-87a1-a0c626137f47"}